    "answer": {
      "short": "All four fail the horizontal line test because different $x$-values give the same $y$-value. Therefore, none has an inverse function.",
      "worked": "The first three graphs are symmetric about the $y$-axis, so opposite nonzero $x$-values give the same $y$-value. The graph of $y=|3x-2|$ is symmetric about $x=\\frac23$; for example, $x=0$ and $x=\\frac43$ both give $y=2$.\n\nEach graph therefore fails the horizontal line test. After swapping $x$ and $y$, the inverse fails the vertical line test and is not a function.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
